# 2. The first major mistake that had to be corrected

My first interpretation collapsed the entire genre list into one supposed hybrid and proposed a genre solution such as “Anatolian Aksak Deep Psych.”

That was wrong because the user had already said:

- this is a **series**;
- this is about **creating our own unique sound**;
- the reference channels were there to be **analysed**, not copied;
- different genre influences could serve different songs and different catalogue functions.

The correct understanding became:

> **one sonic universe / catalogue identity, with different genre centres from track to track.**

The later analysis also established that the reference channels were not merely sonic references. They were relevant to:

- branding;
- catalogue architecture;
- audience targeting;
- listening context;
- channel segmentation;
- distribution strategy;
- creative philosophy;
- consistency versus variation. fileciteturn9file0

A useful distinction emerged:

**Gentleman**  
= broader curator/tastemaker/experimental umbrella.

**Deep & Elegant**  
= more focused listening proposition and sonic destination.

The project therefore needed to learn from the **functional strengths** of those channels without copying their sound.

