# 13. The first fractal model

The earliest fractal idea was highly explicit and mechanical:

- one three-note motif;
- repetitions at multiple time scales;
- each descendant shorter;
- softer;
- brighter;
- same contour;
- vocal echo branching 1→2→4;
- rainfall as macro-arrangement metaphor.

This was a useful first experiment because it translated fractal thinking into concrete musical operations.

The original brief explicitly linked:

- three-note motif → compositional mechanism;
- shorter/softer/brighter → recursive transformation;
- echo splitting → fractal vocal processing;
- rainfall → macro-arrangement. fileciteturn9file3

At that stage, the project explored:

- larger ancestor;
- smaller descendants;
- motif in saz;
- motif in vocal;
- motif in percussion;
- motif in echo;
- same contour at different scales.

