- survival;
- toxic relationship aftermath;
- introspection;
- emotional observation;
- personal imagery;
- layered meaning;
- wordplay;
- occasional humour/double meaning.

The strategy became:

> use existing songs as a source library rather than generate generic Deep House lyrics from scratch.

Long songs can be distilled into:

- central idea;
- strongest image;
- characteristic turn of phrase;
- 2–4 line micro-lyric.

