# 39. The current Suno methodology

The most useful workflow established so far is:

### Step 1 — Define the song’s actual creative objective

Not the whole catalogue again.

### Step 2 — Choose one genre centre

Do not stack all permitted catalogue genres.

### Step 3 — Protect the non-default sound identity

Especially the parts Suno would otherwise resolve generically.

### Step 4 — Put unusual compositional law in Lyrics

Because the Lyrics Assistant has shown better understanding of it than Create Style.

### Step 5 — Use actual lyrics

Because actual lyric content materially affects Suno’s style synthesis.

### Step 6 — Ask Lyricist what it understands

Do not assume.

### Step 7 — Let Create Style propose implementation

Treat its output as Suno’s interpretation, not as authoritative truth.

### Step 8 — Set Style Influence appropriately

Higher than default when establishing the new identity.

### Step 9 — Generate

Do not endlessly polish the prompt before hearing the audio.

### Step 10 — Diagnose audio failures separately

For example:

- sound identity;
- genre drift;
- vocal;
- structure;
- psychedelic character;
- compositional behaviour;
- duration.

### Step 11 — Change only demonstrated failures

Do not rebuild the whole system after every imperfect generation.

### Step 12 — Use successful audio as reference

Eventually the actual successful song becomes more useful than theoretical descriptions.

