# 43. The most important conceptual distinction going forward

The entire project becomes easier if we keep four categories separate:

## A. SERIES DNA

What makes the catalogue recognisably ours.

## B. SONG DNA

What makes one specific track unique.

## C. COMPOSITIONAL TECHNIQUE

Fractal/self-similarity/Reverse Déjà Vu, Aksak, recursive echo, etc.

## D. SUNO IMPLEMENTATION

How we phrase enough of A–C for Suno to produce useful audio.

A technique should not accidentally become series DNA.

A Suno prompt workaround should not accidentally become artistic philosophy.

A successful element from one track should not automatically be repeated across all tracks.

And a failed generation should not cause the entire series identity to be rebuilt.

