# 44. Condensed project statement

If I had to summarise the work **without collapsing it into another genre slogan**, it is this:

> We are building a series of contemporary electronic songs with different genre centres but a coherent higher-order identity: sophisticated, emotionally rich, globally accessible, late-night listening music whose electronic functions are approached through physical, analogue, human and experimentally transformed sound. The creative inheritance of 1960s/70s Anatolian psychedelia is used primarily as an invention philosophy—hybridisation, modal colour, raw analogue mutation and resourceful sound transformation—rather than as obvious regional scenery. Advanced compositional techniques such as self-similar inheritance may be used to make musical material evolve through ancestry, coexistence and adaptation instead of ordinary repetition. Suno is not expected to understand all of this from one compressed Style string; we use Lyrics, Lyricist, Create Style, Style Influence and actual generation as separate parts of an iterative interpretation process, and we correct only what the resulting audio proves has failed.

That is the summary I should have been holding onto instead of repeatedly reconstructing the project from whichever idea happened to be most recent.

